Here's how to implement all three requirements:

## 1 & 2. Intercept Back Navigation

Override `OnBackButtonPressed` in your page:

```csharp
public partial class EditProductPage : ContentPage
{
    private bool _hasUnsavedChanges;

    protected override bool OnBackButtonPressed()
    {
        if (!_hasUnsavedChanges)
            return base.OnBackButtonPressed();

        // Show confirmation (fire-and-forget since override is sync)
        Dispatcher.Dispatch(async () =>
        {
            bool leave = await DisplayAlert(
                "Unsaved Changes",
                "You have unsaved changes. Discard and go back?",
                "Discard", "Stay");

            if (leave)
            {
                _hasUnsavedChanges = false;
                await Shell.Current.GoToAsync("..");
            }
        });

        return true; // cancel the default navigation
    }
}
```

> **Note:** `OnBackButtonPressed` only fires for the **hardware/OS back button** (Android back gesture). It does **not** fire when the user taps Shell's navigation bar back arrow.

## 3. Custom "Cancel" Back Button

Replace Shell's default back arrow with a toolbar item:

```xml
<ContentPage xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/2021/maui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2009/xaml"
             x:Class="MyApp.EditProductPage"
             Shell.BackButtonBehavior="{StaticResource HiddenBackButton}">

    <Shell.BackButtonBehavior>
        <BackButtonBehavior IsVisible="False" />
    </Shell.BackButtonBehavior>

    <Shell.TitleView>
        <HorizontalStackLayout Spacing="8" VerticalOptions="Center">
            <Button Text="Cancel"
                    Clicked="OnCancelClicked"
                    BackgroundColor="Transparent"
                    TextColor="{AppThemeBinding Light=Black, Dark=White}" />
            <Label Text="Edit Product"
                   VerticalOptions="Center"
                   FontSize="18"
                   FontAttributes="Bold" />
        </HorizontalStackLayout>
    </Shell.TitleView>

    <!-- page content -->
</ContentPage>
```

```csharp
private async void OnCancelClicked(object sender, EventArgs e)
{
    if (_hasUnsavedChanges)
    {
        bool leave = await DisplayAlert(
            "Unsaved Changes",
            "You have unsaved changes. Discard and go back?",
            "Discard", "Stay");

        if (!leave) return;
    }

    await Shell.Current.GoToAsync("..");
}
```

## Key Caveats

| Scenario | Covered? |
|---|---|
| Android back button/gesture | ✅ `OnBackButtonPressed` |
| Shell nav-bar back arrow | ✅ Hidden; replaced by "Cancel" button |
| iOS swipe-back gesture | ⚠️ Disable via a custom renderer or handler — MAUI has no built-in API |

To block the iOS swipe-back gesture, you'll need a platform-specific handler:

```csharp
#if IOS
Microsoft.Maui.Handlers.PageHandler.Mapper.AppendToMapping("DisableSwipeBack", (handler, view) =>
{
    if (view is EditProductPage)
    {
        var nav = handler.ViewController?.NavigationController;
        if (nav != null)
            nav.InteractivePopGestureRecognizer.Enabled = false;
    }
});
#endif
```

Register that in `MauiProgram.cs` or in the page's constructor. This gives you full control over all back-navigation paths.
